    FEAT-0001: lock the phone out after three unrecognized fingers
    
    LockedState counts fingers that don't match, and the third one moves
    the phone to LockedOutState. A locked-out phone ignores every finger,
    even the right one, and hides notification text the way a locked phone
    does. Restarting is the only way out: it comes back on as a fresh
    LockedState.
    
    Phone didn't change. Before, a new state meant a new case in all three
    switches, plus a failed-tries counter on Phone that would only mean
    something while the phone was locked.

